<InfoLayout
  path="/press"
  title="Press & Media Kit"
  description="RateKit press kit: boilerplate, brand assets, fact sheet, and founder contact for journalists, bloggers, and anyone writing about RateKit."
  pageTag="Press kit"
  h1="Press & Media Kit"
  pageSub="Everything you need to write about RateKit — boilerplate, logos, fact sheet, and a direct line to the founder."
  breadcrumbLabel="Press"
>
  <div class="highlight-box">
    <strong>Quick summary:</strong> RateKit is a free, no-signup collection of 19 business calculators (ROI, break-even, burn rate, SAFE notes, loan APR, and more) that run entirely in the browser — no data ever touches a server. Everything is also free to embed, free to call as a JSON API, and free to query through an open MCP server.
  </div>

  <h2>Boilerplate</h2>
  <p><strong>Short (one sentence):</strong> RateKit (<a href="https://ratekit.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ratekit.org</a>) is a free, no-signup suite of business calculators for founders and freelancers, with every calculator also available as a JSON API and an MCP server.</p>
  <p><strong>Long (one paragraph):</strong> RateKit is a collection of 19 free business calculators — ROI, break-even analysis, freelance rate, burn rate & runway, LTV:CAC, SAFE note conversion, business loan APR, VAT/GST, self-employment tax, and more — built for founders, freelancers, and startup teams who need a fast, trustworthy number without signing up for anything. Every calculation runs client-side in the browser, so no data is ever sent to a server. Each calculator also ships as a free, no-auth JSON API endpoint, an embeddable widget (<code>?embed=1</code>), and as a tool in an open MCP server for Claude and other AI agents. RateKit is built and maintained by Azat Israilov.</p>

  <h2>Fact sheet</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Launched:</strong> 2026</li>
    <li><strong>Calculators:</strong> 19, covering freelancers, startups, and small business finance</li>
    <li><strong>Pricing:</strong> 100% free, no account, no credit card</li>
    <li><strong>Privacy:</strong> all math runs client-side — no data sent to a server</li>
    <li><strong>Languages:</strong> English and Russian (15 of 19 calculators)</li>
    <li><strong>Developer access:</strong> <a href="/api">free JSON API</a>, <a href="/openapi.json">OpenAPI spec</a>, and an <a href="https://github.com/AIsrail/ratekit/tree/main/mcp-server" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MCP server</a> (18 tools) for Claude and other AI agents</li>
    <li><strong>Embeddable:</strong> any calculator can be dropped into another site with <code>?embed=1</code></li>
    <li><strong>Founder:</strong> Azat Israilov — <a href="https://azatisrail.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">azatisrail.org</a></li>
    <li><strong>Source:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/AIsrail/ratekit" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/AIsrail/ratekit</a> (MIT licensed)</li>
  </ul>

